{"request_sha256": "e4dfd96117a5d253d87627a094776ef385fd3d42aa32d7ddfb4639557307c4a8", "prompt_sha256": "847dd718e56258447ec5fcc89fdaadc9701165d02eab0b51001e616ebc1a0329", "dispatched_prompt_sha256": "379297fe4432d5753f1b99571eec4c75ce581cc850e787e06877c87de224f474", "schema_sha256": "30f41622e6c7560e23f9cf8ab8aee356761b3ddea7cb1a9d1835cabc34f30ac0", "model": "opus", "model_identity_basis": "claude CLI result event modelUsage key: claude-opus-5", "effort": "medium", "status": "ok", "forbidden_tools": [], "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "output_tokens": 6841}, "answer": {"passes": ["fail", "fail", "fail", "unknown", "fail", "fail", "fail", "fail", "pass", "pass"], "defects": ["Crown reads as a sparse spray of ~20 short, straight, hair-thin rays radiating almost flat from a single point (render-0, render-1, render-2); no frond is arching, none droops below the crown base, and the leaflets are pin-thin specks rather than the narrow stiff ranks along a rachis seen in reference-0/reference-1. Frond length is roughly 1/4 of what reference-0 shows relative to trunk length.", "Trunk is distinctly wavy in both seeds: render-0 shows an S-bend with a sharp kink and a second reverse curve in the upper third, render-1 shows two stacked inflections plus a kink; render-2 confirms a serpentine axis at close range. Reference-0 shows a single continuous lean/curve and reference-1/reference-2 a straight vertical stem; the owner priority forbids waviness.", "Trunk surface in render-2 is a smooth, untextured, near-black tapering cylinder with no retained leaf-base stubs, no spiral, no diamond lattice and no fibrous matting; reference-1 and reference-2 show a coarse spiral of projecting wedge-shaped stubs packed with reddish-brown fibre.", "P-BASE (render-3) is an unusable frame: the view is marked hidden and the image shows only a featureless black silhouette against ground and sky with no base, no ground contact and no leaf-base detail, so the required leaf-base-close cell cannot be assessed.", "Leaflet rendering shows heavy stipple/alias breakup (black-and-green speckling along each ray in render-2) well below the finish floor established by anchor-0, where needle masses read as coherent shaded foliage.", "Crown spread is small relative to trunk length and the crown reads as a flat disc/starburst viewed from a low angle rather than the rounded hemispherical shuttlecock of reference-0."], "observations": ["render-0 and render-1 are the same geometry identity at seeds 1 and 42; both show one unbranched stem from ground to a single apical crown, with a widened basal flare where the stem meets the ground.", "No foliage, epiphyte, stub or other growth appears anywhere on the trunk in render-0, render-1 or render-2; the stem is clean from base to crown.", "Trunk colour in the renders is a dark desaturated brown reading almost black in shadow; reference trunks are mid grey-brown to warm reddish-brown. Colour is recorded as an observation, not scored, since the references themselves span a wide tonal range under different light.", "No dead-frond skirt, no petiole sheath colouring, no crownshaft region and no fruit stalks are drawn; the owner states the trunk organs (fn-110) and date cluster (fn-111) are not landed in this pass.", "render-2 (P-TRUNK) is framed on the mid/upper trunk and crown underside; it does not include the ground or the tree base.", "anchor-0 is used only as a finish-quality floor; its spruce morphology carries no weight here.", "The crown in render-2 shows a few rays held steeply upward near the centre and the rest near-horizontal, which is the closest the candidate comes to the reference's stiff-centre/recurved-outer gradation, but no ray curves downward at any point along its length.", "Relative to the inventory, the candidate matches on stem solitariness and bare-trunk cleanliness only; every frond-geometry and trunk-surface core trait is either mismatched or undrawn."], "findings": [{"observation": "Every visible frond in both seeds is a straight, radial, hair-thin ray of roughly uniform length; no downward curvature and no lower drooping tier, against the arching hemispherical rosette with abruptly drooping lower fronds in reference-0 and the recurving fronds in reference-1.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "render-2", "reference-0", "reference-1"], "impact": "blocker", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": "Consistent with frond length and leaflet-size parameters still at their low defaults and with little or no gravity-driven rachis curvature in the frond generator; the mechanism is not established by the images."}, {"observation": "Leaflets appear as isolated speckles a few pixels wide distributed along each ray rather than as two ranks of narrow lanceolate blades giving a plumose V-sectioned frond; even in the closer P-TRUNK framing no individual leaflet blade resolves.", "evidence_ids": ["render-2", "render-0", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "impact": "blocker", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": "Leaflet dimensions may be far below the size at which the rasteriser can form a continuous blade, so the same asset would also produce this stipple at higher resolution; alternative causes (instancing density, alpha coverage) are equally consistent."}, {"observation": "Trunk axis carries multiple reversing bends and at least one sharp kink in both seeds, i.e. wavy rather than straight or gently leaning, and the silhouette narrows and re-widens across those bends.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "render-2", "reference-0", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "impact": "blocker", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": "Could arise from an unclamped per-segment curvature or noise term on the stem spine; not determinable from renders alone."}, {"observation": "The drawn trunk surface is smooth and featureless, carrying neither the spiral diamond lattice of retained leaf bases nor the interstitial fibre mat that reference-1 and reference-2 show as the dominant trunk character.", "evidence_ids": ["render-2", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "impact": "blocker", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": "The owner states trunk organs are scheduled for fn-110; the absence is scored against what is drawn rather than attributed to any mechanism."}, {"observation": "The P-BASE required cell has no assessable content: visibility is hidden and the frame contains only a black silhouette edge, sky and ground.", "evidence_ids": ["render-3", "reference-2"], "impact": "required_unknown", "uncertain": true, "causal_hypothesis": "Camera placement or near-clip for the base view appears to leave the subject unframed or unlit; the cause is not visible in the image."}, {"observation": "Nothing grows on the trunk in either seed, satisfying the owner's third priority; the epiphytic ferns and vines of reference-1/reference-2 are correctly treated as scene features, not species character.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "render-2", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "impact": "supported", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": null}, {"observation": "A single unbranched stem carries one apical crown in both seeds, with no branching anywhere along its length.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "reference-0", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "impact": "supported", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": null}, {"observation": "The basal flare where the render's stem meets the ground is broadly consistent with the widened rooted base of reference-0, though reference detail at that scale is limited and the dedicated base view is unusable.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "reference-0"], "impact": "variation", "uncertain": true, "causal_hypothesis": null}, {"observation": "Pendent fruit bunches, present as a core trait in reference-0, are absent from the candidate. The owner scopes the date cluster to fn-111 and out of this pass, so the trait is reported unknown on grounds of declared scope rather than treated as satisfied or as a blocker for this pass.", "evidence_ids": ["reference-0", "render-0", "render-1"], "impact": "required_unknown", "uncertain": true, "causal_hypothesis": null}, {"observation": "Foliage stipple and the flat near-black trunk shading fall short of the coherent foliage masses and readable surface shading of the fn9 anchor, which sets finish quality only.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-2", "anchor-0"], "impact": "blocker", "uncertain": true, "causal_hypothesis": "May be a sub-pixel geometry/alpha issue rather than a shading-model gap; not separable from these images."}, {"observation": "Both seeds behave the same way on every scored trait, so the failures are not seed-specific; this is a first live pass and any improvement over earlier iterations is not evidence of readiness.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1"], "impact": "supported", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": null}], "coverage": [{"trait_id": "crown-pinnate-arching-fronds", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "render-2", "reference-0", "reference-1"], "explanation": "Reference shows 30-60 long once-pinnate fronds arching outward and downward into a rounded hemispherical crown with recurved older fronds. The candidate draws about 20 short straight rays in a flat starburst with no arching and no lowest-frond droop. Defining mismatch."}, {"trait_id": "leaflet-arrangement-stiff-narrow", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-2", "render-0", "render-1", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "explanation": "No narrow lanceolate leaflets in groups at differing angles are formed; leaflets read as detached speckles giving no plumose V-section and no bristly frond margin. Visible at close range in render-2, so this is a mismatch rather than unresolvable."}, {"trait_id": "trunk-leaf-base-diamond-pattern", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-2", "render-0", "reference-1", "reference-2", "reference-0"], "explanation": "The drawn trunk is a smooth cylinder with no stubs and no spiral diamond tessellation at any scale. Scored on what is drawn; the inventory's caveat that the generator does not yet express it is noted but does not convert a visible smooth surface into unknown."}, {"trait_id": "trunk-fibrous-matting", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-2", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "explanation": "No fibre, husk or shaggy interstitial layer is present on the candidate trunk, which is uniformly smooth and dark."}, {"trait_id": "solitary-columnar-stem", "status": "pass", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "reference-0", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "explanation": "A single unbranched stem carries the crown in both seeds with no branching, and diameter is broadly comparable along the mid-trunk with a basal flare as in reference-0. The waviness of the axis is scored separately under the owner's straight/constant-diameter priority."}, {"trait_id": "fruit-clusters-pendent", "status": "unknown", "evidence_ids": ["reference-0", "render-0", "render-1"], "explanation": "Core in the inventory but evidenced by one reference at one maturity state, and the owner explicitly scopes the date cluster to fn-111 and out of this pass. No supported match exists and the trait is not dismissed; reported unknown on those grounds."}, {"trait_id": "dead-frond-skirt", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "reference-0"], "explanation": "Secondary trait: no collar of dead brown fronds below the living crown is drawn. Not a blocker for this pass."}, {"trait_id": "frond-colour-range", "status": "unknown", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-2", "reference-0", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "explanation": "Variation trait and itself uncertain in the inventory. Candidate foliage is a mid to bright green, inside the deep-green to grey-glaucous span, but the speckled sub-pixel rendering makes the sampled colour unreliable."}, {"trait_id": "petiole-base-orange-sheath", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-2", "reference-1"], "explanation": "Secondary trait: the crown apex shows no petiole bases, no rust-orange sheath fibre and no cut-base tones; rays meet the stem tip directly."}, {"trait_id": "trunk-lean-and-curve", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "render-2", "reference-0", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "explanation": "The inventory admits a leaning S-curved stem as acceptable variation, but the candidate's repeated reversing bends and kinks exceed that range and are explicitly excluded by the owner's straight-or-gently-leaning requirement. Reported fail, not variation."}, {"trait_id": "epiphytes-on-trunk", "status": "pass", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "render-2", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "explanation": "Variation trait treated as a scene feature. Its absence matches reference-0 and satisfies the owner's bare-trunk priority."}, {"trait_id": "trunk-colour-and-weathering", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-2", "render-0", "reference-0", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "explanation": "Secondary trait: candidate trunk is a flat dark brown to near-black with no lighter stub faces, no bleached greys and no weathering variation. Tone alone would be acceptable variation; the total absence of surface differentiation is not."}, {"trait_id": "basal-flare", "status": "pass", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "reference-0"], "explanation": "Secondary and uncertain in the inventory. The candidate widens into a rooted base at ground contact, consistent with the limited reference evidence; the dedicated base view adds nothing."}, {"trait_id": "crown-shaft-absent", "status": "unknown", "evidence_ids": ["render-2", "reference-1"], "explanation": "Secondary. The candidate has neither a smooth green crownshaft nor a stub-covered trunk under the crown, so the distinction the trait draws does not apply to what is drawn and cannot be assessed as match or mismatch."}, {"trait_id": "basal-leaflet-spines", "status": "unknown", "evidence_ids": ["render-2", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "explanation": "Secondary and flagged uncertain in the inventory itself. Candidate leaflets are not resolved at all near the frond bases, so proximal spine-like reduction is unassessable."}, {"trait_id": "crown-silhouette-proportions", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "reference-0", "reference-1"], "explanation": "Variation trait, but the candidate falls outside the observed range in the same direction the owner names: crown spread is only modestly greater than trunk width scaled, and frond length is a small fraction of the visible trunk length rather than the substantial fraction in reference-0."}]}, "raw_events": "{"type":"system","subtype":"init","cwd":"/home/daniel/Projects/telperion/.worktrees/fn-80-the-gap-loops-first-live-run","session_id":"2f9ace83-ceb0-4d86-94be-6976b3696680","tools":["StructuredOutput"],"mcp_servers":[],"model":"claude-opus-5","permissionMode":"default","slash_commands":["deep-research","design","design-sync","dataviz","update-config","verify","debug","code-review","simplify","batch","fewer-permission-prompts","doctor","loop","schedule","claude-api","workflow-authoring","run","run-skill-generator","advisor","agents","auto-mode-setup","autocompact","clear","color","compact","config","output-style","context","effort","fast","heapdump","init","mcp","import","model","__remote-workflow","workflow-launch-exec","reload-plugins","reload-skills","rename","ultrareview","security-review","usage-credits","extra-usage","usage","insights","recap","skill-doctor","goal","design-consent","design-revoke","list-agents","team-onboarding"],"terminal_slash_commands":["doctor","color","reload-plugins"],"apiKeySource":"none","claude_code_version":"2.1.278","output_style":"default","agents":["claude","Explore","general-purpose","Plan"],"skills":["deep-research","design","design-sync","dataviz","update-config","verify","debug","code-review","simplify","batch","fewer-permission-prompts","doctor","loop","schedule","